! mcp_bootstrap_p129.strap -- the tail of the channel-signal supervisor
! and the DISK ARC-ADDRESS arithmetic, printed page 129.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.136, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID EB000356
!  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  129".
!
! THIRTY LINES, TWENTY-EIGHT CARDS.  The card-serial column runs
! EB000356 (line 1) to EB000383 (line 30) and prints TWENTY-EIGHT
! distinct serials for THIRTY lines: EB000364 appears on lines 9 AND
! 10, EB000381 on lines 27 AND 28.  Those two cards each carry TWO
! statements separated by a semicolon, and they are transcribed that
! way below -- "SIC,SDISIC; B,SDISP" and "LX,0,SCW($13); SX,0,
! SCCW($13)".  strap_asm accepts the printed one-card form (it splits
! on ';' at strap_asm.py:1010); IT WAS TESTED BEFORE IT WAS WRITTEN,
! and splitting them into four deck lines would have been a
! substitution nothing on the page asks for.  Counted off the serial
! column, nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render.
! (The volume survey OCR'd 20 rows of this page over 216306.40..
! 216332.00.  It is a LOWER BOUND: it misses line 1 entirely and nine
! more besides.  The page's own thirty line numbers, 1* .. 30*, are
! read directly and are what is used here.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN IS CLOSED AT BOTH ENDS -- which is new for this run
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC, <<< so the hard "SLC,(8)216305.40"
! below ASSERTS the origin rather than checking it (docs/
! transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE
! ARRIVING COUNTER").  But unlike printed p.128, BOTH JOINS HAVE
! INDEPENDENT WITNESSES AND BOTH LAND:
!
!   BACKWARD.  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p128.strap is landed.  Its line 56
!   is a half word at 216305.00, so its counter leaves at 216305.40 --
!   which is exactly this page's line 1 LOCATION.  Independently, p.128
!   line 56 is "BZXCZ,$+1.32", whose target is 216306.40, and that is
!   this page's line 2.  p.128's own deck PREDICTED both ("a full word
!   at 216305.40 puts line 2 at exactly 216306.40"); the prediction is
!   now read off the page.  The card serials agree too: p.128 ends at
!   EB000355 and this page opens at EB000356.
!
!   FORWARD.  Line 30's XW is word-aligned at 216332.00 and is one
!   word, so the counter leaves this page at 216333.00.  The
!   full-volume OCR of PDF p.137 (printed p.130) opens its first
!   storage row at 216333.00 ("216333.00  000003.00 80 215230.00 A0
!   W LOCK  T,0,3.0,STLR").  Nothing falls between the pages.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  The six names this page
! DEFINES are K CS REG, C Q2BIG, K RELAY, C ARC AD, K DISK E and
! K RECEP; none collides with anything in pp.2-98.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-6   the tail of printed p.128's channel-signal supervisor.
!             Line 1 re-arms K SUP CS by setting bit 19 ("-IF SO, NOP
!             ENTRY"), line 2 clears the queue bit the handler just
!             consumed ("-RESET CS QUEUE"), lines 3-4 load a count of
!             16 and store it in $L ("-FAKE CS"), line 5 plants a
!             5-bit field in S TLR+8.9, and line 6 jumps to S FAKE I
!             on printed p.122.
! Line 7      K CS REG, the one-word channel-signal register that
!             printed p.128 stacks into (its lines 38, 41 and 54 all
!             print 216312.00).  THE DEFINING CARD LANDS HERE.
! Lines 8-10  C Q2BIG, the "interrupt queue too big" error exit: load
!             the error code S Q2BIG into $14, save the IC in S DISIC
!             and branch to the dispatcher S DISP.  Lines 9 and 10 are
!             ONE CARD.
! Lines 11-13 K RELAY -- load the MCP return address out of the file
!             area table and branch through it, "B,0.0($8)".
! Lines 14-24 C ARC AD, the arc-address arithmetic.  Line 14 pulls the
!             original count out of the control word; line 15 clears
!             S HS ECH; lines 16-17 test the final CW count for zero;
!             lines 19-21 ask whether the number of arcs is an integer
!             and round up by one if not ("M+1"); lines 22-24 add the
!             result to S ARC AD and store the sum into BOTH S ARC AD
!             and S CU ARC.  Line 18 is a COMMENT CARD (EB000372, no
!             LOCATION, no BINARY): its text "-$L HOLDS NO OF ARCS
!             WHICH EQUALS" runs on into line 19's comment.
! Lines 25-29 K DISK E, the disk error path: force a locate on the
!             next I/O by setting the whole 18-bit S ARC AD field to
!             ones, copy S CW into S CCW, and rejoin K GATE.  Lines 27
!             and 28 are ONE CARD.
! Line 30     K RECEP XW,0 -- the receptor's index word, a full word
!             of zeros, referenced from printed pp.122, 125 and 126.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY EXTERNAL IS LANDED SOMEWHERE ELSE.  NOT ONE IS NEW.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This is unusual and it is worth saying plainly: fifteen symbols are
! referenced and not defined here, and every one of them is already
! carried by a landed deck at the value this page's binary demands.
! Nothing below is back-derived from this page alone.
!
! SCOMRG  215001.00  p.103 line 8 "S COM RG XW,(8)520000.".  Carried
!                    only so S HS ECH can be written as p.103 writes it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! SHSECH  215001.01  p.103 line 11 "S HS ECH SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+.1".
!                    FULLY OBSERVED here: line 15 is a VFL connective,
!                    so its printed "215001.01" is a BIT address and
!                    bit 1 is read, not conventional.
SHSECH  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.1
! The five FILE/UNIT AREA TABLE field symbols are copied VERBATIM from
! the landed decks that define them, mode and length included, because
! a SYN's data description is part of what the referencing rows
! compile.  All five values are fully observed here: a field symbol
! lands in the address field as a bit address.
! SCW     3.0   p.102 line 14 "S CW SYN(BU,64),3.0 -CONTROL WORD".
!               Line 27 prints 000003.00 and line 14 prints
!               000003.34 for "SCW.28" -- 28 decimal bits = .34 octal,
!               so the word AND the offset arithmetic are checked.
SCW     SYN(BU,64), 3.0
! SCCW    4.0   p.102 line 15 "-COPIED CONTROL WORD".  Lines 16, 28.
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0
! SRETAD  5.0   p.101 line 18 "-RETURN ADDRESS IN MCP".  Line 11
!               prints 000005.20, where .20 is register 8 and the
!               symbol's own offset is 0.
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0
! SCUARC  6.0   p.102 line 19 "S CU ARC SYN(BU,18),6.0 -CURRENT ARC".
!               Line 24 prints 000006.00 8D.
SCUARC  SYN(BU,18), 6.00
! SARCAD  0.32  p.99 line 52 "S ARC AD SYN(BU,18),0.32 -ARC ADDRESS
!               (DISK)".  Lines 22, 23 and 26 all print 000000.40,
!               and 0o40 = 32 decimal: the bit offset is READ.
SARCAD  SYN(BU,18), 0.32
! SDD     0     p.108 line 10 "S DD SYN(BU,7),0 -DISK DENSITY *
!               0-LOW, 1-HIGH".  See the note on line 14 below: this
!               page pins 55-SDD only MODULO 128, so the value 0 comes
!               from p.108, not from here.
SDD     SYN(BU,7), 0
! STLR    215230.00  landed by pp.116/117/118/128; printed p.117 line
!                    12 is the defining card, "S T LR DRZ(BU,64),29".
!                    Line 5 prints "STLR+8.9" as 215240.11 -- 8 words
!                    plus 9 decimal bits = .11 octal -- the same
!                    half word printed p.128 line 20 prints.
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! SFAKEI  215721.40  >>> THE LAST CHARACTER IS THE LETTER I. <<<
!                    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p122.strap line 202 DEFINES
!                    it -- "SFAKEI L(BU,4),SEQUIP($10),-19" at its
!                    !SYM 215721.40 -- and the volume OCR carries that
!                    same card ("215721.40 ... S FAKE I L(BU,4),
!                    S EQUIP($10),-19").  This page's line 6 prints
!                    215721.50 00, and a B contributes 0o10 to the
!                    printed offset field, so the target half word is
!                    .40 and bit 18 IS checked.
SFAKEI  SYN, (8)215721.40
! KGATE   215746.40  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p122.strap line 181 and
!                    p.127 line 396, both at .40; p.123 line 348 is
!                    the defining label row ("KGATE BZB,SUNSUP($11),
!                    JKGATE").  Lines 25 and 29 print 215746.50 00.
KGATE   SYN, (8)215746.40
! KSUPCS  216242.40  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p128.strap DEFINES it (its
!                    line 4, "K SUP CS NOP,K MT CSQ", !SYM 216242.40).
!                    Line 1 here prints 216242.63 80 001000.36 F0 --
!                    the SAME two half words p.128 line 39 prints for
!                    its own "CM0000(BU,1),K SUP CS.19", with only the
!                    connective differing.  Bit 19 is the branch-enable
!                    bit of that NOP; line 1 turns it ON where p.128
!                    line 39 turns it off.
KSUPCS  SYN, (8)216242.40
! SDISP   217372.00  landed by pp.119, 120 and 124.  Line 10 prints
!                    217372.10 00.
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0
! SDISIC  217451.40  landed by pp.103, 119, 120 and 124, every one of
!                    them off a printed "SIC,S DISIC".  Line 9 prints
!                    217451.40 80, so the half word IS checked.
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40
! SQ2BIG  (16)0708.0  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap line 289,
!                    "SQ2BIG SYN,(16)0708.0 -78 INTERRUPT QUE TOO
!                    BIG".  Hex 0708 = 1800 decimal = 0o3410, and line
!                    8 here prints 003410.35 01 -- an EXACT, fully
!                    observed match of an error code read off a
!                    different page in a different radix.  This is the
!                    strongest single corroboration on the page.
SQ2BIG  SYN, (16)0708.0
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NOTHING WAS SUBSTITUTED.  FOUR PRINTED FORMS WERE TESTED FIRST.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The forms that looked likely to be assembler gaps were each tried AS
! PRINTED before anything else was considered, and strap_asm accepts
! all four:
!   * "KF(BU,64),$Z"   (line 19) -- a KF with a data description; the
!     only KF in the test suite before this was p.45's bare "KF,Q CMA".
!   * "BAE, $+1.32"    (line 20) -- BAE appears nowhere in strap_asm.py
!     by name; it is generated by the branch tables.
!   * "+, S ARC AD($10),64"  (line 22) -- a bare "+" connective with a
!     space after the comma.
!   * "XW,0"           (line 30) -- an XW WITH an explicit zero
!     operand, where printed p.128's line 23 is a bare "XW,".
! The two semicolon cards (lines 9/10 and 27/28) were tested the same
! way.  NO ASSEMBLER LIMITATION WAS HIT ON THIS PAGE.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS: WHAT WAS SETTLED, AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs like every other: its own heading
! prints "LOCATICN", the header's time clock prints "0C054C41", and
! line 2's second half word prints 001000.00 as "001000.CC".  A round
! glyph in a LOCATION or an octal BINARY field is a 0 with certainty
! (C is not an octal digit) and every one is read as 0.  The glyphs
! that are NOT in an octal field were each settled on something else:
!
!   * C Q2BIG (line 8).  The second word's first glyph is a Q, not a
!     G or a C: at 1200 dpi it carries a DESCENDING TAIL below the
!     baseline at the lower right, which line 7's "REG" G (a bar
!     INSIDE the bowl, no descender) does not.  >>> THE SECOND
!     WITNESS IS WEAKER THAN IT LOOKS AND IS NOT A SECOND PAGE. <<<
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p123.strap line 342 carries "CQ2BIG
!     SYN,(8)216313.0", but its own note (line 146) shows it took the
!     name from the OCR of THIS card -- the same row, not an
!     independent reading of another page's ink.  So the Q rests on
!     this page's ink at 1200 dpi, supported by the OCR of this row
!     and by p.107's operand S Q2BIG ("-78 INTERRUPT QUE TOO BIG",
!     whose English puts a QUEUE in the neighbourhood).
!   * C ARC AD (line 14) / S ARC AD / S CU ARC.  "ARC" is a real token
!     in this listing, not a damaged "ORC": p.85 line 12's comment
!     "-ORIGINAL ARC" prints it in English, p.99 line 52 defines
!     "S ARC AD ... -ARC ADDRESS (DISK)", and this page's own line 18
!     comment reads "-$L HOLDS NO OF ARCS WHICH EQUALS".  C ARC AD's
!     address 216316.00 is corroborated by
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p122.strap line 183, which SYNs CARCAD at
!     216316.0 off its own line 48 "BXE,C ARC AD".
!   * S FAKE I (line 6).  See the SYN note above; the letter I is
!     p.122's reading of the defining card, not this page's ink.
!   * 55-SDD (line 14).  >>> BOTH GLYPHS ARE D. <<<  Re-rendered at
!     1800 dpi and upscaled, each has the straight vertical LEFT stem
!     and squared corners of a D; a C or a 0 is round with no stem
!     (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "C vs D, AND THE ORACLE CANNOT
!     CATCH IT").  The wider crop confirms there is no fourth
!     character and that "-ORIGINAL COUNT TO ACC" is a separate
!     comment field, so the operand really is the expression 55-SDD.
!   * K DISK E (lines 17, 26).  THE ONLY NAME ON THIS PAGE WITH NO
!     WITNESS ANYWHERE ELSE -- see UNRESOLVED below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 14's "55-SDD" IS PINNED ONLY MODULO 128
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The printed second half word is 022033.60 50.  Varying ONLY the
! final operand through strap_asm, the value that reproduces it is 55
! -- and so is -73.  The two differ by 128, so the offset field that
! carries it is seven bits and THE CHECK CANNOT DISTINGUISH 55 from
! 55-128.  What it establishes is 55-SDD == 55 (mod 128), i.e. SDD is
! 0 modulo 128 bits.  SDD = 0 exactly comes from printed p.108 line
! 10, which is a different page and a real second reading; this page
! on its own would also admit SDD = 2.0 or -2.0.  Said here so that a
! passing !CHECK is not read as more than it is.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION on lines 1, 7 and 24 -- "216305.40 *",
! "216312.00 *", "216325.40 *".  printed pp.3, 37, 103, 120 and 128
! carry the same mark and it was left unexplained on each.  Line 7 is
! the page's only DRZ, which might suggest a reservation marker, but
! lines 1 and 24 are an ordinary VFL connective and an ordinary store.
! It changes no compiled bit and nothing here depends on it.
!
! THE IBM TYPO IS TRANSCRIBED AS PRINTED.  Line 23's run-on comment
! reads "64-SUM TO STORAGE IN" with no space before the dash, and line
! 24's "64 - S ARC AD AND S CU ARC" with one: the same sentence,
! punctuated two ways on consecutive cards.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COVERAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Thirty printed lines.  Line 18 is a comment card and emits nothing.
! Line 7's DRZ gets NO !CHECK: its printed "000001.00" is the
! RESERVATION COUNT in the BINARY OUTPUT column, not storage contents,
! and there is nothing deposited for the oracle to read -- printed
! pp.84, 109 and 114 give their DRZ rows no !CHECK for exactly this
! reason.  Its LOCATION is checked, by "!SYM KCSREG 216312.00".
! THE REMAINING TWENTY-EIGHT ROWS ALL CARRY A !CHECK and all six
! symbols a !SYM.
!
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py was run with this deck alongside the
! repository's: 968 symbol definitions, NO symbol spelled two ways.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

        SLC, (8)216305.40

        CM1111(BU,1),KSUPCS.19        ! line  1  -IF SO, NOP ENTRY
        CM0000(BU,1),KCSREG($11)      ! line  2  -RESET CS QUEUE
        LCI,7,16                      ! line  3  -FAKE CS
        SC,7,$L                       ! line  4
        CM0101(BU,5),STLR+8.9,-13     ! line  5
        B,SFAKEI                      ! line  6
KCSREG  DRZ(BU,64),1                  ! line  7
CQ2BIG  LVI,$14,SQ2BIG                ! line  8  -LOAD ERROR CODE AND
        SIC,SDISIC; B,SDISP           ! lines 9 and 10, ONE CARD EB000364
KRELAY  LV,8,SRETAD($12)              ! line 11
        SC,7,1.0($13)                 ! line 12
        B,0.0($8)                     ! line 13
CARCAD  L(BU,18),SCW.28($13),55-SDD   ! line 14  -ORIGINAL COUNT TO ACC
        CM0000(BU,1),SHSECH           ! line 15
        LX,0,SCCW($13)                ! line 16  -TEST IF FINAL CW COUNT IS ZERO
        BZXCZ,KDISKE                  ! line 17
!                                       line 18  COMMENT CARD, EB000372:
!                                       "-$L HOLDS NO OF ARCS WHICH EQUALS"
        KF(BU,64),$Z                  ! line 19  -IS NO OF ARCS AN INTEGER
        BAE, $+1.32                   ! line 20  -IF YES, BRANCH
        M+1(BU,64), 8.0               ! line 21  -IF NOT, ROUND UP BY ONE
        +, SARCAD($10),64             ! line 22  -ADD THIS TO S ARC AD AND RETURN THE
        ST(BU,18),SARCAD($10),64      ! line 23  -SUM TO STORAGE IN
        ST(BU,18), SCUARC($13),64     ! line 24  - S ARC AD AND S CU ARC
        B,KGATE                       ! line 25
KDISKE  CM1111(BU,18),SARCAD($10)     ! line 26  -FORCE LOCATE ON NEXT I/O
        LX,0,SCW($13); SX,0,SCCW($13) ! lines 27 and 28, ONE CARD EB000381
        B,KGATE                       ! line 29
KRECEP  XW,0                          ! line 30

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, read off PDF p.136 (300 dpi for the page, 900
! dpi for the LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT columns, 1200 dpi for the
! NAME column, 1800 dpi for line 14's "55-SDD" and lines 17/26's
! "K DISK E").
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!  LINE  LOCATION      BINARY OUTPUT                      NAME      STATEMENT                      COMMENT                              CARD
!   1*   216305.40 *   216242.63 80  001000.36 F0                   CM1111(BU,1),K SUP CS.19       -IF SO, NOP ENTRY                    EB000356
!   2*   216306.40     216312.00 8B  001000.00 F0                   CM0000(BU,1),K CS REG($11)     -RESET CS QUEUE                      EB000357
!   3*   216307.40     000020.17 02                                 LCI,7,16                       -FAKE CS                             EB000358
!   4*   216310.00     000010.17 50                                 SC,7,$L                                                             EB000359
!   5*   216310.40     215240.11 80  005071.52 F0                   CM0101(BU,5),S TLR+8.9,-13                                          EB000360
